"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[2336],{32336:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"gajd-2-pds","title":"Guide 2. Long-Term Savings Program: Launching the LSP Without the Risk of Losing Subsidies","sourceFingerprint":"4f5e8d968ad6e0eee8e3f37d50ab7f315a4d8af328d029c8ac4b3cd6313124e8","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"*Volume II: Capital Protection: 20 Years Against Inflation*  \\n*Section: Practical Investor Guides*"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"# Workshop: Launching the Long-Term Savings Program Without the Risk of Losing State Support"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"> \\"Any state subsidy is effective only when the investor knows the hidden terms of the contract precisely and does not allow bureaucratic traps to nullify the accumulated result.\\""},{"id":"b004","markdown":"The Long-Term Savings Program (PDS) is a hybrid instrument: a citizen accumulates capital through an accredited NPF, while the state budget co-finances contributions for up to 36 000 ₽ annually over the first ten years. Below is a strict seven-stage algorithm that allows you to claim the entitled premium and tax preferences in full."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"## Step-by-Step Onboarding Procedure"},{"id":"b006","markdown":"### Stage 1. Feasibility Audit of Participation\\nBefore opening an account, verify compliance with three criteria:\\n1. **Planning horizon:** you will not need the spare funds for current needs for at least 15 years (or until reaching the age of 55 for women and 60 for men).\\n2. **Official income level:** maximum yield is achieved with a monthly income of up to 150 000 ₽. If income exceeds this threshold, the state subsidizes only 25 kopecks for every deposited ruble, which significantly reduces the relative yield of the instrument.\\n3. **Availability of a near reserve:** short-term goals on a horizon of up to 5 years are already covered by bank deposits, high-yield savings accounts, and the balance of an IIS-3."},{"id":"b007","markdown":"> **Attention Marker:** the tax base for the social deduction is capped at a limit of 400 000 ₽ per year in total for Type-3 IIS, pension agreements, and PDS. If you allocate the maximum 400 000 ₽ to IIS-3, you will not be able to claim an additional personal income tax refund via PDS (however, the right to state co-financing of up to 36 000 ₽ per year remains fully intact)."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"### Stage 2. Comparison and Filtering of Operators (NPFs)\\nRegistration takes place through non-state pension funds (NPFs). Mandatory organization verification checklist:\\n* **Regulator licensing:** verify the presence of an active entry in the register of financial market entities on the Bank of Russia portal (`cbr.ru`).\\n* **DIA guarantee system:** presence of the fund in the state system for guaranteeing the rights of participants (capital insurance coverage under PDS is 2.8 million ₽).\\n* **Retrospective returns:** examine asset management results over an interval of 5–7 years based on official regulator summaries. Returns for a single successful year are not representative.\\n* **Digital infrastructure:** assess the usability of the fund\'s mobile application or integration with your daily online banking."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"### Stage 3. Legal Execution of the Agreement\\nYou can execute the agreement online via the single portal \\"Gosuslugi\\" (mechanism available from October 1, 2025), directly on the selected NPF\'s website, or at a branch of an agent bank."},{"id":"b010","markdown":"> **Attention Marker:** previously accumulated funded pension (OPS) is permitted to be transferred into the body of the PDS. The transferred pension balance will begin to be invested by the fund; however, it is not recognized as a fresh contribution and does not entitle you to receive a state co-payment for the current period."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"### Stage 4. Calculation and Launch of Optimal Contributions\\nThe minimum threshold for co-payment accrual is **2 000 ₽ per calendar year**. If you contribute less, the state support for the calculation period is forfeited."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"To claim the maximum **36 000 ₽ per year**, rely on the formula corresponding to your salary bracket:"},{"id":"b013","markdown":"| Average Monthly Official Income | Required Annual Contribution | Monthly Payment | Annual Co-payment from the State |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Up to 80 000 ₽** | 36 000 ₽ | 3 000 ₽ | 36 000 ₽ (1:1 ratio) |\\n| **From 80 000 to 150 000 ₽** | 72 000 ₽ | 6 000 ₽ | 36 000 ₽ (1:2 ratio) |\\n| **Over 150 000 ₽** | 144 000 ₽ | 12 000 ₽ | 36 000 ₽ (1:4 ratio) |"},{"id":"b014","markdown":"*Practical solution:* set up a recurring auto-debit on the day following your salary payout. Depositing amounts below the calculated limits is not prohibited—the state will calculate the co-payment strictly in proportion to the contributed funds."},{"id":"b015","markdown":"### Stage 5. Monitoring Subsidy Transfers\\nNo special requests need to be submitted: the NPF reports centrally to the program operator. State funds for the preceding calculation year are credited to the account during the summer period (traditionally between May and July). Your task is to open the statement in mid-summer and verify the receipt. In the absence of a transaction, an official inquiry is submitted to the fund\'s support service."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"### Stage 6. Claiming the Tax Refund\\nThe personal income tax refund is processed using a scheme similar to that of the IIS: through the taxpayer\'s account on the FNS website via a 3-NDFL declaration or through a simplified application based on data transmitted by the operator."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"### Stage 7. Monitoring Early Termination\\nPremature termination of the agreement without grounds established by law leads to the complete cancellation of state support and the return of only the so-called \\"surrender value,\\" calculated with a reduction discount according to the fund\'s rules."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"*Legitimate exceptions for withdrawing the full amount without penalties:*\\n* The need to pay for expensive medical procedures (according to an approved list).\\n* Death of the family breadwinner."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"*Note:* Switching from one NPF to another with transfer of funds does not nullify accumulated co-financing."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"## \uD83E\uDDEE Calculation in the Margins"},{"id":"b021","markdown":"Let\'s analyze the scenario of engineer Mikhail (official earnings — 75 000 ₽ per month).\\n* **Monthly tranche:** 3 000 ₽ (36 000 ₽ per year).\\n* **State co-financing:** 36 000 ₽ per year (1 to 1 ratio).\\n* **Tax refund at the 13% rate:** 36 000 ₽ \xd7 13% = 4 680 ₽.\\n* **Total for 1 year of personal contributions of 36 000 ₽:** the investor receives 72 000 ₽ in the account plus 4 680 ₽ refunded to the bank card (excluding the NPF investment return).\\n* **In total over the 10 years of the support program:** the net co-payment from the budget will reach **360 000 ₽** solely due to disciplined auto-payments."}],"terms":[{"id":"npf-operator","term":"LSP Operator","definition":"a non-governmental pension fund managing savings program accounts."},{"id":"strakhovka-pds","term":"LSP Insurance of 2.8M ₽","definition":"a state guarantee of the safety of funds in the LSP provided by the DIA (Deposit Insurance Agency)."},{"id":"dorogostoyashchee-lechenie","term":"Special Life Situation","definition":"a qualifying event (medical treatment) allowing early withdrawal of funds from the LSP without penalty."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"q1","q":"What is the maximum annual amount of state co-financing of contributions to the Long-Term Savings Program (LSP)?","options":["Up to 36,000 rubles per year during the first 10 years of participation","No more than 5,000 rubles once upon opening the contract","The state doubles any deposited amount without restrictions"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Legislation on the LSP sets the limit of the state subsidy at up to 36,000 rubles per year."},{"id":"q2","q":"What is the insurance coverage limit for savings in the LSP under the DIA state insurance system?","options":["1.4 million rubles, just like for a standard bank deposit","2.8 million rubles (including personal contributions, state support, and investment returns)","Funds in non-governmental pension funds are not insured at all"],"correct":1,"explanation":"State DIA insurance for LSP accounts is 2.8 million rubles—exactly twice as high as for a standard bank deposit."},{"id":"q3","q":"In which special life situation does the law permit early withdrawal of funds from the LSP without losing the right to co-financing?","options":["Purchasing a new car or a vacation trip","Paying for expensive medical treatment according to the list established by the Government of the Russian Federation or loss of a breadwinner","Any investor\'s request upon submitting an application 3 days in advance"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A special life situation (expensive medical treatment from the Government-approved list) allows early withdrawal of funds without forfeiting subsidies."}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);